{{// 🩹 Chibi GLM patch, for GLM 5.x, Flash included: five lines at the end of the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate, where GLM listens best, and in the plan, about 134 tokens where the full edition spends 238. They print twice, so this is Chibi's largest patch. Everyone agrees or pushes back as their card would and helps, praises, advises or comforts you only as far as the card and their bond allow; the answer covers your whole move, the character's main concern first, a true line keeps its size and the answer moves on; steadying filler becomes the thought itself, though one may stay as an answer. Two lines answer what GLM 5.3 Flash did deeper into a chat and keep every mechanic confirmed live. Pushback: a character says what they hold plainly and cuts a clause on what your view or their own last line is not; a refusal stays a plain no, the one exception the 🖋️ Anti-Slop Codex and the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate allow now. Restate: a repeat or bare label of the line before, with or without an intensifier, is cut, and so is any phrase marking speech as on the record, honest, clear or said first, which the gate's Register line misses because it only checks how speech opens; nervous stammers stay. To fit, Chibi left out 'the next act carries the weight' after a cut restatement. Native thinking stays one quick pass through The Logic Core's lines. GLM Flash users switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too; its Runs line handles the clipped short sentences. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{setvar::ariaPatchLines::5}}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Person: agree or push back per card; help, praise, advise or comfort {{user}} only as card and bond allow.
- Replies: answer {{user}}'s whole move, main concern first; a true line keeps its size, then something new.
- Filler: steadying or self-talk filler becomes its thought or an act; one stays as an answer.
- Pushback: say what they hold plainly and cut a clause on what {{user}}'s view or their last line is not; a refusal stays a plain no.
- Restate: cut a repeat or bare label of the line before, intensified or not, and any phrase marking speech as on record, honest, clear or said first; stammers stay.}}

