{{/if}}Native reasoning: one pass, a terse bullet per plan line or step, no drafts, then stop.{{setvar::ariaPatchLines::1}}{{setvar::ariaPatchGate::- Filler: steadying or self-talk filler becomes its thought or an act; one stays as an answer.}}

{{// 🩹 Chibi MiMo V2.6 Pro patch: about 71 tokens of text where the full edition spends 93. It brings back each character's usual mood and interests, keeps secrets to their own topic (the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate keeps them hidden until you uncover them), keeps names, colours, values and filled gaps the way the chat first set them, and stops counts, ages, images and paragraph layouts from coming back unless the story changed them. Its Contrast rule is now the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate's own, for every model. Run it with 🏷️ Logic Core Tags ON and native reasoning off; if no plan shows up, switch to the system-role twin of The Logic Core. MiMo V2.6 Flash uses 🩹 MiMo V2.6 Flash instead. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
