{{// 🩹 Chibi MiMo V2.6 Flash patch, for the model u/trashhaul caught writing slop the Pro patch couldn't stop: about 78 tokens of text plus two plan and gate lines (about 65) where the full edition spends 191 and 70. Newcomers give a name and one reason for being here, and anyone's card details show later, one at a time, through what they do. A run of 'not this, not that' before the real word is cut by the 🚪 Last-Mile Gate's Contrast rule, for every model. Narration sentences keep their own subject and verb and run five words or more. Characters react to what actually happened rather than to what kind of talk it is, and names, colours and values stay as first set. The full edition states the introduction and flow rules twice, in the text and in the plan and gate lines; Chibi keeps them once, in those lines (the speech exceptions of Flow are left to the Codex's Chop rule). Switch 🔦 Flash Gate ON too, since it carries the rule against repeated demands, keep 🏷️ Logic Core Tags ON with native reasoning off, and try Temperature 0.8. MiMo V2.6 Pro uses 🩹 MiMo V2.6 Pro instead. Use one model patch at most.}}{{trim}}
{{#if .ariaHardener}}{{setvar::ariaHardPlan::{{getvar::ariaHardPlan}}
- Lulls: one card interest, by act or question to someone present.
- Kept: names, colours, values, filled gaps as first set; counts, ages, images, paragraph layouts return only if the story changes them.
- Reactions: answer what was said or done, claims and stakes, by stance or act; dodge only when the card dodges.}}{{addvar::ariaHardN::3}}{{else}}Lulls: one card interest, by act or question to someone present.

