{{// 🧠 Chibi Logic Core: ARIA's planning step, rewritten from Realistic Frankenstein's Micro chain of thought in Chibi size. The AI plans in the first person as the game master instead of a helpful assistant, takes creative risks, writes every line in order, keeps you and every NPC on the same footing, and carries each NPC's act through, nervous cards aside; with 🔞 Adult Context on, its Mode line plans a sexual, violent, cruel or dark beat in full. Lines that other modules add (Mode, Fate, Bonds, Ledger, Layers, the 🧪 hardener's Claims and moved patch rules, patch lines, Tally, Joins) join the plan and its line count; the wiring is the full edition's. With Logic Core Tags off the AI plans inside its own reasoning and stops at go. With them on, or with the Gemini 4 Argon Thinking Tags Enforcer entry, every reply opens with the plan inside the tags (The Logic Core itself starts on that tag, so a model that copies its own last message starts its reply on the tag SillyTavern folds away) and the gate gets a one-line reminder, which is printed by the Gate as its last line; when Reduce Reasoning is also on, Reduce Reasoning comes after it. The phrases the echo-cleaning regex scripts match (opens the reply, then / closes on the line after go / The reply starts on the line after that / Nothing above go enters the reply / Every response starts with) stay word for word. Leave this ON; if your model still overthinks, switch Reduce Reasoning on alongside it. Keep both Logic Cores above the gate in the list.}}{{trim}}
